    ],
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "transformers-integration",
        "title": "Load EXL3 layers through Transformers quantization hooks",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "patch_transformers writes the exl3 entries into AUTO_QUANTIZER_MAPPING and AUTO_QUANTIZATION_CONFIG_MAPPING and assigns QuantizationMethod.EXL3 = 'exl3'. Exl3Config stores that value as quant_method. This is process-local registration, not a new model architecture implementation.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_374256cc61ae414fa55f8c34e09df96b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "get_modules_to_replace requires model.name_or_path to be a directory, scans its safetensors headers and considers only torch.nn.Linear instances. Replacement requires trellis plus either su or suh and either sv or svh. Other modules remain untouched. The collection's group check tests names, not tensor dimensions.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_374256cc61ae414fa55f8c34e09df96b",
              "call_8d54601e5b6b4532859bf13dac2fd4de"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Discovery translates a model.language_model. module prefix to language_model.model. for checkpoint lookup while retaining the original module path for replacement. A scalar transcription verified that the hardcoded slice index 21 exactly removes the former prefix.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_74bc44df4ff141b1b988b1232275116a"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Exl3HfLinear builds registered meta buffers from header shape and torch_dtype metadata for trellis, optional bias and the packed/unpacked factor alternatives. Its separate one-element meta weight is only a dtype placeholder, not a reconstructed dense weight. replace_modules recursively inserts wrappers and records them for post-load finalization.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_374256cc61ae414fa55f8c34e09df96b",
              "call_8d54601e5b6b4532859bf13dac2fd4de"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The documented 4096-input, 1024-output example uses 256 by 64 tiles of 16 by 16 weights, with 48 sixteen-bit storage words per tile. Scalar arithmetic confirmed 786432 words and exactly three packed bits per weight; factor and bias storage are additional overhead.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_74bc44df4ff141b1b988b1232275116a"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "finalize casts unpacked factors and bias to FP16, then constructs LinearEXL3 with config=None, FP16 output and transformers_fix=True. Compared with the existing Linear.load_exl3 and convert_exl3 construction sites, it enables the CPU packed-sign workaround but omits their mcg/mul1 propagation. LinearEXL3's existing datatype and required-factor assertions still execute.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_374256cc61ae414fa55f8c34e09df96b",
              "call_8fe2f56c631a459cb48ecc453b1ebeda",
              "call_2cf5e61d6ef74060997a72b7076ddf3b",
              "call_4d6b4ee2ada2450c97981fc8bbbe646d"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The wrapper saves the input dtype, calls the inner forward with x.half() and an empty parameter dictionary, then casts the result back. Unlike the existing Linear.forward caller, it exposes neither reconstruct nor output-dtype overrides and adds no ExLlama module-level softcap/post_scale processing. The inherited default reconstructs for more than 32 flattened rows; otherwise it uses direct EXL3 GEMM. Reconstruction allocates an FP16 inner matrix and uses native reconstruction and hgemm rather than retaining a permanent dense weight.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_374256cc61ae414fa55f8c34e09df96b",
              "call_043c49af47444751a0c5310a4eb2700f",
              "call_4d6b4ee2ada2450c97981fc8bbbe646d",
              "call_8fe2f56c631a459cb48ecc453b1ebeda",
              "call_8d4746bc2d664aa78842eff205e05a89"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The before-load hook conditionally sets the config supplied through kwargs to tie_word_embeddings=False; it does not unconditionally mutate model.config. The after-load hook finalizes every recorded replacement, clears the list and returns the model. The source therefore establishes the mutation and ordering, not whether every Transformers loading path supplies that config argument.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_374256cc61ae414fa55f8c34e09df96b",
              "call_bc324407446c409db289a6b099cf001e",
              "call_4d456af2191f4606bc836fdb2aa0ffa7"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Existing SafetensorsCollection callers include configuration loading, variant collections, compilation and the index utility. Configuration can supply a load method or variant map; compilation reads payloads and closes handles after groups; the index utility uses headers only. The adapter follows the header-only use, explicitly closes its collection on the normal path, and leaves actual checkpoint payload loading to Transformers.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_2ea1c4261edb41e394631fe0140f368f",
              "call_86968aaa43b9470383f86c1e0bb7655e",
              "call_55414f2339e94a9eace28dc241204a14",
              "call_055bd00672764d0f8946780bc1396099",
              "call_5de2ea119fae4527a763c121faac2a38",
              "call_374256cc61ae414fa55f8c34e09df96b"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "decoder-metadata-not-forwarded",
        "origin": "authoring_observation",
        "status": "suspected",
        "classification": "defect",
        "description": "The Transformers wrapper drops optional per-layer codebook multiplier tensors supported by the existing EXL3 loader.",
        "trigger": "A local checkpoint contains an otherwise matching Linear tensor group encoded with a nonzero mcg or mul1 multiplier.",
        "expected_behavior": "Preserve the stored multiplier when constructing LinearEXL3, or reject the unsupported codebook explicitly.",
        "actual_behavior": "Discovery accepts the group, but Exl3HfLinear registers neither multiplier buffer and finalize passes neither argument. LinearEXL3 therefore stores zero multipliers and selects the original decoder in both direct GEMM and reconstruction, rather than the checkpoint's selected codebook.",
        "locations": [
          {
            "commit": "bcaa636f66973eac4ac071ad25ef31e8586a02dc",
            "path": "exllamav3/integration/transformers.py",
            "symbol": "Exl3HfLinear.finalize"
          }
        ],
        "source_evidence": [
          "call_374256cc61ae414fa55f8c34e09df96b",
          "call_4d6b4ee2ada2450c97981fc8bbbe646d",
          "call_77f9f0e1519b4631af98672fde95cf5e",
          "call_8fe2f56c631a459cb48ecc453b1ebeda",
          "call_101b083f457c4ec8b9d608040f8a05a3",
          "call_8d4746bc2d664aa78842eff205e05a89"
        ],
        "verification": [
          {
            "method": "source_inspection",
            "description": "Whole-parent-tree search found no existing Exl3Hf definitions. The task's before-load hook constructs wrappers and its after-load hook directly calls finalize. Compared that path with both existing LinearEXL3 construction sites, quantizer tensor emission and native decoder selection.",
            "evidence": [
              "call_0cc4217b3465433ba665e21132c37226",
              "call_2cf5e61d6ef74060997a72b7076ddf3b",
              "call_374256cc61ae414fa55f8c34e09df96b",
              "call_4d6b4ee2ada2450c97981fc8bbbe646d",
              "call_77f9f0e1519b4631af98672fde95cf5e",
              "call_101b083f457c4ec8b9d608040f8a05a3",
              "call_8d4746bc2d664aa78842eff205e05a89"
            ],
            "limits": "No affected checkpoint was loaded. Reach is limited to replaced layers carrying experimental multiplier metadata; original-codebook layers do not trigger this discrepancy. Transformers' treatment of the unregistered checkpoint keys was not executed."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "summary": "Adds explicit Transformers EXL3 registration, header-driven Linear replacement, post-load finalization and a generation example. The adapter remains local-directory/GPU-only and omits existing experimental decoder metadata."
  },
